{parent=a}

Pair the first and last terms of the <arithmetic series>. There are $500$ pairs, each summing to $1001$, so
$$
\boxed{N_1=\frac{1000\cdot1001}{2}=500\,500.}
$$

= b
{parent=10}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <finite geometric series> has eleven terms, from $2^1$ through $2^{11}$. With common ratio $2$,
$$
\boxed{N_2=2\frac{2^{11}-1}{2-1}=4094.}
$$
Counting the powers explicitly avoids omitting the final $2048$ term.

